    "def-frobenius-characteristic-map": {
      "citations": [],
      "derivations": [],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The Definition covers the empty partition: for n=0 the only partition is the empty partition, p_empty=1 and z_empty=1, so the defining sum has the single term f(empty) and ch(f)=f(empty) is a complex number in Lambda_C^0."
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The Definition is a sum of scalar multiples f(rho)p_rho/z_rho; the zero class function has f(rho)=0 at every cycle type, so ch(0)=0 in Lambda_C^n, and the zero of each degree is consistent with the degreewise definition on cf_S."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The Definition fixes one normalization with no free parameter: z_rho is the centralizer order from [[thm-centralizer-cardinality-from-cycle-type]] and the coefficients are f(rho)/z_rho; for n=1 and the trivial class function, ch(1)=p_1/z_(1)=p_1 since z_(1)=1."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The Definition requires only rho|-n; z_rho is positive because it is a product of positive terms, so no division degenerates, and the family p_rho/z_rho is a Q-basis of Lambda_Q^n by [[prop-power-sums-form-a-rational-not-integral-stable-basis]], which makes the finite sum well defined."
        },
        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The Definition is stated for every n>=0, including the lower endpoint n=0 (handled by the empty case) and with no upper bound; n=0 gives ch: cf(S_0)=C -> Lambda_C^0=C, and no endpoint convention beyond p_empty=z_empty=1 is needed."
        },
        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The Definition states that no choice principle is used; its data are a finite sum over the finite set of partitions of n and the previously published basis, so no selection from a family of nonempty sets occurs."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The Definition is not an iff statement: it defines a map and records the sufficient condition that rational-valued class functions land in Lambda_Q^n, with the converse direction belonging to the later dictionary theorems."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The Definition asserts no converse: the claim that every virtual character of S_n is rational- and integral-valued is proved later on this page, not in the Definition."
        }
      ],
      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-18",
        "notes": "Definition reviewed in full against its six direct dependency statements: complex class functions, rational power-sum basis, Hall orthogonality, cycle-type classes, centralizer cardinality and S_0 convention. Finite sum ch(f)=sum_rho f(rho)p_rho/z_rho is well typed in Lambda_C, with positive z_rho and no arbitrary choice. At n=0 it is the identity C→C; ch(0)=0 and imaginary-valued functions remain in the complex codomain. Rational/integral virtual-character assertions are explicitly deferred to the later dictionary theorem. Macdonald (7.2), printed p. 113, has the same normalization. No defect found."
      }
