          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "def-partition-young-diagram-and-conjugate-partition",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **partition of $n$** is a finite weakly decreasing sequence $\\lambda=(\\lambda_1,\\dots,\\lambda_k)$ of positive integers with $\\lambda_1+\\cdots+\\lambda_k=n$.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "d11",
          "claim": "In Q[x_1,...,x_N][[t]], log and exp are inverse between 1+tQ[x][[t]] and tQ[x][[t]], and exp(A+B)=exp(A)exp(B). The geometric product is exp(sum_k p_k t^k/k); finite coefficient extraction yields h_d^(N)=sum_{rho|-d}p_rho^(N)/z_rho.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "given"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d21",
          "claim": "The defining finite polynomials specialize under setting added variables to zero (h_d has degree d and p_k degree k). Thus the identities at every rank give the stable identity in Lambda_Q^d.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F3",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d31",
          "claim": "h_lambda factors as the product over rows of the one-row expansions.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d41",
          "claim": "List the row cycle lengths in decreasing order to reconstruct each partition rho^(j) from its multiplicities. Collecting the product coefficients gives N(lambda,rho)/z_rho, where equal-length cycles are distinct and each row is labelled.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F4",
            "F5",
            "step 3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d51",
          "claim": "The empty partition case and the one-row case h_d=sum_{rho|-d}p_rho/z_rho, completing the lemma.",
          "step": "5.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "step 2.1",
            "step 4.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Step 5.1 treats n=0: lambda=rho=empty, the empty product gives h_empty=1, z_empty=1 and N(empty,empty)=1, so both sides are 1."
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "If no matrix of nonnegative multiplicities satisfies the fixed row sums and cycle counts, N(lambda,rho)=0 (for example lambda=(1,1), rho=(2)). The definition requires equal total sizes; no extension to unequal sizes is asserted."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Step 5.1 computes the one-row case lambda=(d): N((d),rho)=1 for every rho|-d, giving h_d=sum_{rho|-d}p_rho/z_rho; for d=1 this reads h_1=p_1."
